<title>USA: Rubin says Dole tax cut plan will hurt.</title>
<headline>Rubin says Dole tax cut plan will hurt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said Republican presidential candidate Bob Dole's economic proposals amount to &quot;a very large tax cut with no plausible way of paying for it.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;It will explode the deficit, undermine the economy,&quot; Rubin said on ABC Television's &quot;This Week With David Brinkley&quot; program.</p>
<p>Rubin said that Dole's plan for a $550 billion tax cut over six years would put upward pressure on interest rates.</p>
</text>
